    "formats": { "national": "0YX XXX XXX", "international": "+252 YX XXX XXX (trunk 0 dropped)" },
    "patterns": [
      { "label": "Fixed line — Mogadishu (021) and Federal Member State codes (02X)", "national": "021 XXX XXX", "international": "+252 21 XXX XXX" },
      { "label": "Mobile — Hormuud, Somtel, Telesom (6X, 7X–9X)", "national": "061 XXX XXX", "international": "+252 61 XXX XXX" }
    ],
    "examples": [
      { "type": "fixed-line", "e164": "+25221123456", "international": "+252 21 123 456", "national": "021 123 456", "note": "Mogadishu — area code 21" },
      { "type": "mobile", "e164": "+25261123456", "international": "+252 61 123 456", "national": "061 123 456", "note": "Mobile — 61 is a Hormuud range" }
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Somali numbering was largely unregulated between 1991 and the establishment of the National Communications Authority in 2017; NSN length is inconsistent across operators, so length-based validation is unreliable.",
      "Fixed-line area codes were standardised in 2021 around an 02X series for the Federal Member States.",
      "Somaliland, which declares independence but is internationally recognised as part of Somalia, also uses +252 — the country code does not distinguish the two."
    ],
    "sources": [
      "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telephone_numbers_in_Somalia",
